{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power-conversion efficiencies of 24.84% in small cells and 21.46% in mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in scalable flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates why early humans settled only briefly in specific desert regions despite abundant water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Arabia's Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found no lithic artifacts or knappable stone at 55 of 125 sites with paleolake deposits. The results indicate that early human settlement required both water and accessible stone for tool production, not water alone, challenging previous dispersal models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artifacts or knappable stone were found at 55 sites with paleolake deposits",
    "Settlement patterns tracked co-occurrence of water and lithic raw materials rather than water alone",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, improving site discrimination accuracy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that lithic raw material availability, not water, was a critical constraint on early human dispersal into arid regions, refining models of Pleistocene human migration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction in human ILC3s decreased PRKAR1A, enhancing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. These findings reveal PKA signaling as critical for ILC3 maintenance and IL-23-induced inflammation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduced ILC3s and increased enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction in human ILC3s decreased PRKAR1A, promoting gut inflammation via PKA signaling"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a pivotal regulator of ILC3 homeostasis and identifies IL-23 as a key driver of pathological PKA activation in gut inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates iron's melting temperature and electrical resistivity under Earth core pressures using microsecond pulsed Joule heating in diamond anvil cells. Over 300 reproducible melting measurements reveal a shallow melting curve, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K at 200 GPa. The findings suggest a relatively cold core-mantle boundary (3430 K) and low adiabatic outer core heat flow (9.8 TW), indicating thermal convection could power the geodynamo before inner core formation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A shallow melting curve for iron at 200 GPa, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K",
    "Inferred core-mantle boundary temperature of 3430 K",
    "Low adiabatic outer core heat flow of 9.8 TW"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical constraints on Earth's core thermal structure, suggesting thermal convection alone could drive the geodynamo prior to inner core formation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility between cocatalysts in alkaline systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides/oxynitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility as a bottleneck for pure water splitting over Ta3N5",
    "Development of RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a fundamental design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting in nitride/oxynitride systems, providing mechanistic insights for advancing solar-driven water splitting technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. Post-recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. These findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates acute skin inflammation to chronic obesity levels",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and Nlrp3/Il1b expression mediate HFD-induced inflammatory amplification",
    "Persistent chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells cause exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite dietary recovery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a dietary window mechanism where transient metabolic states can durably reprogram tissue-specific immune memory, providing insights into how short-lived physiological changes impact long-term inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated early Bundibugyo virus outbreak dynamics in the Democratic Republic of the Congo using case records and human mobility data. It demonstrated that human movement drove spatial expansion from May 10th to June 1st, 2026, with 12 health zones and 49 health areas reporting cases. The early doubling time was approximately 10 days, indicating rapid spread and informing intervention strategies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Human mobility drove spatial expansion of Bundibugyo virus cases across health zones",
    "12 health zones and 49 health areas reported positive cases between May 10th and June 1st",
    "Early doubling time estimated at ~10 days"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides insights into the rapid spatial spread dynamics of Bundibugyo virus, highlighting the role of human mobility in early outbreak expansion and informing timely public health interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how 4f electron filling influences bonding evolution in lanthanide single-atom catalysts across the series. Using structurally uniform catalysts, researchers identified a dual-periodic trend in binding energies, increasing from La to Eu and Gd to Yb. The half-filled 4f7 configuration at Eu-Gd transition causes abrupt changes, while consistent crystal-field effects enable robust linear relationships across coordination environments. These findings establish an intrinsic 4f-electron-regulated framework for lanthanide reactivity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support binding energies increases from La to Eu and Gd to Yb",
    "The half-filled 4f7 configuration induces an abrupt transition between Eu and Gd",
    "Consistent crystal-field effects enable robust linear relationships between binding and bonding energies across diverse coordination environments"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes an intrinsic 4f-electron-regulated bonding framework for understanding lanthanide reactivity and guiding catalyst design."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how Celtic languages spread across Iron Age Europe using ancient genomic data from 4,587 individuals. By analyzing Bronze and Iron Age populations, it identifies three key demographic processes: Steppe-related ancestry migration around 4400 BP, a Bronze Age movement from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion of eastern central European ancestry from 3200-2800 BP. The findings suggest the eastern central European migration is most parsimonious for Celtic language dispersal, though language shifts may not directly track genetic changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry arrived via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Eastern central European ancestry expanded westward from 3200-2800 BP, affecting France, the British Isles, northeastern Iberia, and Italy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genomic evidence supporting a specific demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal in prehistoric Europe, resolving debates about homelands and dispersal routes through ancient population analysis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study constructed a comprehensive single-cell and spatial transcriptomics atlas of the estrogen receptor-positive ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) tumor microenvironment using 159 patients' samples. It identified 9 cell types and 60 cell states, revealing fibroblast, vascular, and basal cell remodeling around DCIS regions, along with immunosuppressive ducts supporting preinvasive growth. The findings highlight early TME alterations that persist through invasive progression.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of 9 cell types and 60 cell states in estrogen receptor-positive DCIS tumor microenvironment",
    "Remodeling of fibroblasts, vascular, and basal cells encircling DCIS regions",
    "Presence of immunosuppressive ducts supporting preinvasive cancer growth"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a detailed map of early tumor microenvironment alterations in preinvasive breast cancer, revealing persistent changes that may inform understanding of invasive progression mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates using a nonfullerene acceptor-iridium coordination polymer (BTP-N-Ir) as a triplet sensitizer in organic solar cells to enhance triplet exciton utilization. The approach involves creating a ternary blend where triplet excitons transfer to an intra-moiety excited state of the acceptor, generating free charges. The polymer demonstrates a small singlet-triplet energy gap, enabling efficient triplet exciton generation and transfer, achieving a record 20.37% power conversion efficiency in triplet-sensitized organic photovoltaics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BTP-N-Ir exhibits a small singlet-triplet energy gap facilitating long-lived triplet exciton generation",
    "Triplet excitons transfer to intra-moiety excited (i-EX) states of the acceptor, dissociating into free charges",
    "The ternary OSCs with this triplet sensitizer achieve a record 20.37% power conversion efficiency"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a novel triplet-exciton transfer pathway via intra-moiety excited states, significantly advancing triplet utilization strategies for high-efficiency organic photovoltaics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used in vivo CRISPR screening to identify synergistic gene pairs that enhance CAR-T cell efficacy against tumors. It discovered NR4A1-SOCS3 double knockout as a potent combination, improving metabolic fitness and mitochondrial activity in CAR-T cells. The modified cells showed superior tumor control across models without safety issues, outperforming single and dual-gene edits.",
  "key_findings": [
    "NR4A1-SOCS3 double knockout enhances CAR-T cell metabolic fitness and mitochondrial activity",
    "NR4A1-SOCS3 DKO CAR-T cells achieve superior tumor control across multiple models",
    "The pair outperforms single and dual-gene modifications in efficacy and safety"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a high-throughput method for identifying synergistic intracellular targets to engineer more effective CAR-T therapies by overcoming intrinsic T cell regulatory mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated the long-term circulation of an Andes virus (ANDV) lineage in northern Patagonia, linking it to a 2026 cruise ship hantavirus pulmonary syndrome (HPS) outbreak. Retrospective analysis revealed a common ANDV lineage spanning HPS cases from 2018 to 2025 in this region, with person-to-person transmission in the 2018 outbreak. The cruise ship outbreak's infection source remains unresolved, underscoring the need for enhanced viral surveillance in ANDV-endemic areas.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A single ANDV lineage caused HPS cases in northern Patagonia from 2018 to 2025",
    "The 2018 outbreak involved person-to-person transmission",
    "The 2026 cruise ship outbreak's infection source could not be resolved with current data"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a persistent ANDV lineage in northern Patagonia, demonstrating long-term circulation without widespread community transmission and highlighting the challenges in tracing outbreak origins within endemic regions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates electromigration-driven carbon transport in cobalt and nickel, revealing direct current-induced graphite precipitation, significant isotope fractionation (12C enrichment up to ∼88 at%  13C), and composition-dependent thermal properties. Raman and ToF-SIMS analyses confirm isotope-sensitive transport mechanisms with enrichment factors of 1.29-1.62. The findings demonstrate current-directed material formation with isotope fractionation and thermal property variations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Direct current drives interstitial carbon transport in cobalt and nickel, leading to graphite precipitation 8-10 mm from the cathode",
    "Raman and ToF-SIMS show 12C enrichment up to ∼88 at% 13C with enrichment factors of 1.29-1.62",
    "Composition-dependent thermal conductivity variations observed via frequency-domain thermoreflectance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes electromigration as a mechanism for isotope-selective material formation in metals, providing insights into current-directed transport and fractionation processes relevant to understanding interstitial solute dynamics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the synthesis and properties of a two-dimensional reticular triaxial molecularly woven polymer network using C3-symmetric macrocycles and dative B-N polymerization. The material demonstrates topological chirality, robust mechanical properties, and selective separation capabilities for aromatic/aliphatic compounds, showcasing higher-order weaving's potential for advanced functional materials.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Synthesis of a two-dimensional reticular triax. woven polymer network via C3-symmetric macrocycles and dative B-N polymerization",
    "The material exhibits topological chirality and robust mechanical properties",
    "It enables selective separation of aromatic and aliphatic compounds"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that higher-order triaxial molecular weaving can create functional materials with unique topological properties and separation capabilities, advancing the design of next-generation functional polymers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates early Homo sapiens hunting practices in Arabia 125,000 years ago using a Middle Paleolithic site in Saudi Arabia. Analysis of stone tools, residues, and megafauna reveals in situ tool production, animal and plant processing, and evidence of poison residues from Acokanthera schimperi in hunting weapons. The findings indicate complex hunting strategies involving hafted weapons targeting diverse ecosystems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Presence of Levallois tool production and megafaunal remains at a 125,00:00-year-old Arabian site",
    "Stone tool residues and biomarkers show processing of palms, tubers, trees, and shrubs",
    "Poison residues from Acokanthera schimperi indicate hafted weapon tips used in hunting"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research provides evidence of sophisticated hunting techniques and ecological adaptation by early Homo sapiens in Arabia during the Middle Paleolithic period."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing mechanical properties in soft magnetic alloys without compromising magnetic performance. The researchers developed an Fe-Co-Ni-Nb multicomponent alloy with coherent ordered nanoprecipitates exhibiting exceptionally high antiphase boundary energy (325 mJ/m²). The alloy achieved high saturation magnetization (151 Am²/kg), low coercivity (49 A/m), and high ductility (28% elongation), outperforming existing soft magnetic alloys.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fe-Co-Ni-N: A multicomponent alloy with coherent ordered nanoprecipitates of high antiphase boundary energy (325 mJ/m²)",
    "Achieved high saturation magnetization (151 Am²/kg) and low coercivity (49 A/m) while maintaining high ductility (28% elongation)",
    "The alloy surpasses existing soft magnetic alloys in mechanical and magnetic properties"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a strategy to simultaneously optimize mechanical strength and magnetic properties in soft magnetic materials through high antiphase boundary energy nanoprecipitates."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates glioblastoma cellular plasticity using scDORI, a deep-learning framework analyzing single-cell multi-omic data from over a million cells. It reveals a structured regulatory program where asymmetric activator-repressor interactions govern state transitions. Low-plasticity states, like neuronal-like configurations, are actively maintained by safeguard repressors, with MYT1L identified as a key regulator that suppresses alternative fates and enhances therapy response.",
  "key_findings": [
    "scDORI infers enhancer-driven gene-regulatory networks at single-cell resolution in glioblastoma",
    "MYT1L acts as a safeguard repressor maintaining neuronal-like states by silencing alternative fates",
    "MYT1L restriction reduces tumor growth and invasion while loss accelerates malignant progression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes that cellular plasticity in glioblastoma is governed by a dynamic balance of activators and repressors, highlighting safeguard repressors as potential therapeutic targets for cancers with therapy-resistant phenotypic switching."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines strategies to resolve power transmission grid failures by analyzing stakeholder alignment through experimentation, learning, and current regulatory frameworks. It identifies that collaborative approaches leveraging existing technologies and regulations can improve grid resilience without requiring new infrastructure. The research suggests that coordinated stakeholder engagement enhances transmission system stability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Collaborative stakeholder engagement improves power transmission grid resilience",
    "Existing regulatory frameworks and technologies can be leveraged for grid stability",
    "Experimentation and learning processes facilitate alignment among stakeholders"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that integrating stakeholder collaboration with current regulatory and technological resources provides a practical pathway to enhance power transmission system resilience without additional infrastructure investment."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines closed-loop bioelectronic systems that integrate sensing, adaptive computation, and targeted therapy without human intervention. It assesses recent advances in functional materials, transducers, and control architectures enabling autonomous operation across neurological, cardiovascular, metabolic, and wound healing applications. The study highlights progress from preclinical to clinical validation, noting chronic stability, machine learning generalization, and wireless power delivery as key challenges.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed-loop systems now achieve clinical validation in multiple disease areas including neurological, cardiovascular, metabolic, and wound healing contexts",
    "Functional materials must form stable, mechanically matched interfaces with living tissue for long-term implantation",
    "Chronic interface stability and wireless power delivery at clinical tissue depths remain critical challenges for scalable implementation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes a comprehensive framework for translating closed-loop bioelectronic systems from preclinical research to clinically validated therapies, addressing material compatibility, real-time control, and scalability barriers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates cost-effective pathways for China's carbon neutrality by integrating hydrogen derivatives into its energy system. Using high-resolution renewable deployment, provincial power operations, and hydrogen transportation routing across 29 regions, the research demonstrates that hydrogen-based transitions reduce transition costs by $10.7 trillion compared to renewable-only strategies, achieving negative carbon abatement costs ($-6.15/ton) and eliminating oil imports.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Hydrogen derivatives reduce overall transition costs by $10.7 trillion relative to renewable-only pathways",
    "The approach achieves negative carbon abatement costs ($-6.15/ton) and eliminates external oil imports",
    "Hydrogen-based strategies align with over 50% of China's 2023 trade surplus"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a scalable framework for cost-effective carbon neutrality in major economies through hydrogen derivatives, offering insights applicable to global energy transition challenges."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether thermal infrared radiation from thermogenic plants attracts beetle pollinators. Using thermal imaging and controlled experiments, researchers observed beetle behavior around plants emitting heat. Results indicate beetles are drawn to specific thermal signatures, suggesting thermal cues play a role in plant-pollinator communication.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Beetles respond to thermal infrared signals emitted by thermogenic plants",
    "Thermal imaging confirmed beetles' attraction to plant heat signatures",
    "Thermal cues may mediate plant-pollinator interactions beyond visual cues"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that thermal signals can function as an alternative communication channel in plant-pollinator interactions, expanding understanding of pollination mechanisms beyond visual and olfactory cues."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses shallow aluminum utilization in aqueous batteries by developing intermetallic anodes that enable bulk aluminum incorporation via electrochemically driven Ni-Al alloying. The approach uses high-surface-area Ni powder to achieve kinetic accessibility beyond surface-limited deposition. Results show reduced charge-transfer resistance, stable symmetric-cell operation, and long-duration cycling with 98.6% capacity retention after 6000 hours at 0.1 mA cm-2, demonstrating practical viability for aqueous aluminum batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Electrochemically driven Ni-Al alloying enables bulk aluminum incorporation in aqueous batteries",
    "High-surface-area Ni powder anodes achieve kinetic accessibility for alloying beyond surface-limited deposition",
    "The anode design supports stable symmetric-cell operation with 98.6% capacity retention after 6000 hours at 0.1 mA cm-2"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes intermetallic anodes as a viable strategy for achieving bulk aluminum storage in practical aqueous batteries, overcoming key limitations in aluminum-based energy storage systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated using AI on consumer smartwatch data to detect hypertension without traditional blood pressure cuffs. The approach involved analyzing photoplethysmography and accelerometry waveforms from 196 participants. Results showed the AI method achieved sensitivity of 65.8%, specificity of 90.0%, and positive predictive value of 80.6% compared to gold-standard ambulatory monitoring, indicating potential for opportunistic screening in the general population.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AI analysis of smartwatch photoplethysmography and accelerometry waveforms detected hypertension with 65.8% sensitivity",
    "The AI method demonstrated 90.0% specificity and 80.6% positive predictive value against ambulatory BP monitoring",
    "The approach outperformed initial office BP screening in sensitivity (55.3% vs. 65.8%) while maintaining similar specificity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a consumer-friendly method for hypertension detection using existing smartwatch data, potentially enabling widespread early screening without clinical equipment."
}
